{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1218160-help-me-understand-how-to-play-mage-the-awakening","id":1218160,"title":"Help me understand how to play Mage The Awakening","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-13T02:26:59-07:00","id":1218160,"title":"Help me understand how to play Mage The Awakening","content":"So I've read MtAw2e from cover to cover and I have not a single idea on how to go about running or playing Mage. Reading the book didn't give me any plot hook or story inspiration and I feel like I barely understood what the game is about, though I'm extremely intrigued by the premise and I simply NEED to play the game, what to do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T02:33:44-07:00","id":1218161,"title":"","content":"Read an Actual Play or two, as well as some of the fiction in the Fallen World Chronicle Anthology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T04:33:02-07:00","id":1218172,"title":"","content":"As fairly new to mage, only started getting into it with 2ed, I can agree that it's a game with a high bar to get into. I usually don't read the novels and stuff to the book, but I think that first, the fiction about the Interfector in the Core book is a great story. But it was the stories in the Fallen World Chronicle Anthology that actually got me starting to understand the game. I highly recommend the Dramitc failure podcast The Hanged Man, which is a pretty new one, only like four episodes yet about their MtA chronicle.<br /> <br /> Also, relax about the game structure. It's a pretty investigative game, but works on different premise then most other ones. The information the players can get out from the start is pretty enormous compared to most games.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T07:35:32-07:00","id":1218203,"title":"","content":"There is a useful thread in another Forum that I seem to keep linking to:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?815371-Mage-the-Awakening-2e-Seeking-Advice-Running-Mage-for-the-First-Time\" target=\"_blank\">[Mage: the Awakening 2e] Seeking Advice - Running Mage for the First Time</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T05:00:31-07:00","id":1218477,"title":"","content":"The book doesn't give a good idea on &quot;but what can I do imo&quot;. The way I see Mages main activities can be divided in two categories, Politics (cabal, order of consilium level) and Exploration of the fallen world. This second category is very broad, it might mean visiting other realms, spelunking into ruins, hunting for artifacts or just inspecting the general weirdless of the CoD setting. These two pillars can be connected, Mages frequently bicker about how (and who) to deal with a particular phenomenon, because every Mage worth his salt wants to lay his hands on a piece of occult knowledge.<br /> <br /> So in essence, I think the correct way would be thinking what local occult phenomena happen in the neighborhood or what your character is interested in (ghosts? artifacts? mapping leylines? cryptids? the tribe of troglodites living at the back of the local walmart?) and build from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T17:31:13-07:00","id":1218741,"title":"","content":"Mage is Scooby Doo if Scooby Doo was a dark drama and Shaggy was Sorcerer Supreme.. If you can come up with ideas for a Scooby Doo episode you can twist them into a plot for a Mage Adventure. Ultimately, Mage is a game about a group of investigators that try to solve mysteries. That mystery could be a literal investigation like &quot;What is haunting the old amusement park&quot; or it could be a more scientific mystery (if you view the Arcane as a type of science), like &quot;what made everyone sick at the football game&quot;. But in these mystery stories the investigators can break the rules of reality.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is an over-simplification, but it is a good starting point to get your head in the game.<br /> <br /> My Mage game, (which is on hiatus until Signs of Sorcery comes out) is set in the 1920s. The players are faculty members at Harvard University and are the leaders of the Metaphysical Studies Society, a campus club and a Mystery Cult. They travel the world solving mysteries. They found a bridge in West Virginia that was being built for malign Arcane reasons and stopped the Mage responsible for it then bound a spirit to the bridge to eventually warn of when the bridge would fail. They freed Nikola Tesla from the influence of an Abyssal Assistant and saved him from being killed by Banishers. Just to name a few things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T08:35:35-07:00","id":1218928,"title":"","content":"I do recommend Boston Unveiled's Beast of Burden story as a good starting point for any Chronicle. It's a Mystery that has exploration, role-playing and action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T22:49:03-07:00","id":1219188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1218160-help-me-understand-how-to-play-mage-the-awakening#post1218160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've read MtAw2e from cover to cover and I have not a single idea on how to go about running or playing Mage. Reading the book didn't give me any plot hook or story inspiration and I feel like I barely understood what the game is about, though I'm extremely intrigued by the premise and I simply NEED to play the game, what to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll need someone to play Storyteller and someone to be a mage.<br /> <br /> If you can't or don't want to build your own setting, you can start with an existing one, such Salamanca, Spain. It comes with its own plot hooks that lead to an increasing scale of danger that should fit with the advancement of the player. There are mysterious books appearing in the library. The players can be hooked into this through their Order, which acts as a broad description of their interests and motivations (an Adamantine Arrow might be charged to protect a certain book, as someone foretold something happening with it, while a Mystagogue might have to find and detail the books as soon as they arrive before the Guardian comes and sanctions aspects of it).<br /> <br /> It builds up pretty much like a story, with the PCs as protagonists. One event leads to another, ratcheting up the 'action' (which doesn't have to be action movie action, it can be more like a crime movie putting together evidence and figuring things out) as things build to a climax. For instance in the fiction that goes with the book, Outis a Guardian of the Veil, is sent to a New York consilium to 'enact justice' by punishing a mage responsible for the deaths of other mages. In the course of their duties, they interview the accused (who has given herself up) and go about doing their own investigation, knowing that an admittance of guilt isn't necessarily the entire story.<br /> <br /> So from a game perspective, he'd be doing mostly social and mental stuff, talking with the accused and other characters, then going out and doing his own investigative work, using his own skills supplemented by Mage Sight and liberal use of spells, while balancing his own issues and political pressures put on him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T23:26:25-07:00","id":1219194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1218160-help-me-understand-how-to-play-mage-the-awakening?p=1219188#post1219188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So from a game perspective, he'd be doing mostly social and mental stuff, talking with the accused and other characters, then going out and doing his own investigative work, using his own skills supplemented by Mage Sight and liberal use of spells, while balancing his own issues and political pressures put on him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Outis' story also has an example of Legacy use in it, I believe. He uses one of the 11th Questions' Attainments (Matter/Time) detailed in the book to turn dried blood back to wet, to allow the friendly neighborhood Space Adept to figure out who it belongs to.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18038-traffichazard","name":"TrafficHazard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18038_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T13:15:07-07:00","id":1219372,"title":"","content":"Why does the blood have to be wet to do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T13:26:52-07:00","id":1219382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1218160-help-me-understand-how-to-play-mage-the-awakening?p=1219372#post1219372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does the blood have to be wet to do that?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think he samples it, but can't remember. Might just be convenience thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T13:55:41-07:00","id":1219402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1218160-help-me-understand-how-to-play-mage-the-awakening?p=1219382#post1219382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think he samples it, but can't remember. Might just be convenience thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's not freshening it to allow Locksmith to check its sympathies; the flakes becoming a droplet of blood is the first part of the visual that concludes with it becoming an image of the person it came from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I open my palm, revealing the tiny flakes of dried blood, fragments of an old death and a new one. I cast a spell, separating the two, then another, calling on the laws of Time and Death to reverse the passage of years. The old blood, the blood Gee found when she first moved to the Squat, liquefies into a droplet on my palm. It grows, shimmering and warping into the image of the person it once was.<br /> <br /> \u201cSecond question,\u201d I ask. \u201cWho\u2019s this?\u201d </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T18:49:28-07:00","id":1219505,"title":"","content":"Right, I misremembered. Although I'm pretty sure once bodily fluids dry, their connection becomes weaker. But I could be wrong about that too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18038-traffichazard","name":"TrafficHazard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18038_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T19:01:57-07:00","id":1219510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrafficHazard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1218160-help-me-understand-how-to-play-mage-the-awakening?p=1219505#post1219505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, I misremembered. Although I'm pretty sure once bodily fluids dry, their connection becomes weaker. But I could be wrong about that too.</div> </div> </div> </div>As blood or a fragment of whatever ages it will lose Sympathy with its source eventually, that's probably what you're thinking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T16:00:29-07:00","id":1220644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrafficHazard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1218160-help-me-understand-how-to-play-mage-the-awakening?p=1219505#post1219505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, I misremembered. Although I'm pretty sure once bodily fluids dry, their connection becomes weaker. But I could be wrong about that too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it works that way in the Dresden Files...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}